Composed mutation for the ai-meta#257 serve-readiness gate.

Two compiling defects at once, one from each of the two pieces whose evidence
this gate consolidates. The point of composing them is that the consolidated
gate must catch BOTH families of assertion, not just whichever one it happens to
run first — a bundle that only fails on one of them would be reporting the other
family's checks as evidence when they cannot fail.

  1. src/metrics_server.rs (from playbooks/261-tier-query-service) — reinstate
     the silent fall-back to the pod-local store WHILE STILL REPORTING
     `tier_query_source: service`. The label stays honest-looking and the bytes
     come from another store. This is the defect PR 4 closes, in the form that
     is invisible to any check reading the label alone.

  2. src/ehdb/tier_service.rs (from playbooks/260-tier-service-metrics) — drop
     the `record_tier_service` call for `append` and nothing else. The append
     still succeeds and the store still grows; only the request-path signal
     disappears. A gate asserting "the store grew" passes this.

Apply with `git apply --3way mutation.patch`, build, and expect a NON-ZERO exit
from `gate.sh service`. Revert with `git apply -R --3way mutation.patch`.

